; The MEMBER-position spelling of the fixed-inner `T / null` collapse (`[v: true / null]`; equally
; a map value `{? k: true / null}` and a table value `{* uint => (true / null)}`) is REJECTED
; GRACEFULLY at the member-level collapse site (`rust_type`'s two-arm null checks), the role-sibling
; of the rule-level site pinned by tests/robustness/choice_fixed_null_collapse.cddl.
;
; It is a genuinely separate site, not a duplicate: a member has no rule name to quote back, so the
; message is role-generic ("used as a member or element type"), and the guard must return an inert
; placeholder rather than registering nothing — the record path around it still expects a type back
; for the field. WHY the shape has no representation, and what to write instead, are shared text
; with the rule-level site so the two spellings of one defect cannot drift apart in what they teach.
;
; Without this guard the shape aborts generation at the same internal render invariant the
; rule-level spelling hit; the neighbouring supported shapes (`[v: bool / null]`, `[v: uint / null]`)
; are unaffected and still lower to `Option<bool>` / `Option<u64>` members.
a = [v: true / null, x: uint]
